            <description><![CDATA[
<h3>Ask your AI assistant</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>MCP server</b> — Claude, Cursor and other MCP clients can now ask MRRDock for your MRR, ARR, revenue, subscriptions and MRR history, in total and per platform. Set it up in one line: see “Use it with Claude” in the README.</li>
<li><b>Your keys stay put</b> — API keys never leave the macOS Keychain: MRRDock calls the platforms itself and hands over only the numbers. The tools only read.</li>
</ul>
            ]]></description>
